! Template for tests/integration/driver_restart/test_driver_restart.py.
!
! Grid, DOMAIN and DYNAMICS are based on tests/integration/nesting/namoptions.1012,
! but runmode here is RUN_COLDSTART (1), not TEST_NESTING_PROLONG (1012): that
! nesting runmode dispatches straight into an in-solver unit test and returns
! before the time loop ever runs (see execute_runmode_actions in
! src/program.f90), whereas this test needs a real, fixed-timestep
! time-marching run that writes and restarts a driver record.
!
! No &NESTING block and no nesting BCs: BCxm/BCym are left at their periodic
! defaults (BCxm_periodic = 1, BCym_periodic = 1, see src/modglobal.f90).
! libm = .false. (no IBM) and ladaptive = .false. (fixed dt = dtmax), so that
! restart parity is bitwise, as required for the byte-identity assertions in
! test_driver_restart.py.
!
! BCbotm/BCtopm are set to freeslip (1) rather than left at the BCbotm
! default (BCbotm_wf = 2, wall function), and iwallmom = 1 (no wall function)
! rather than its default 2 (Werner-Wengle): with ltempeq = .false. (this
! case does not solve temperature), checkinitvalues in src/modstartup.f90
! forces the *neutral* wall function (iwallmom==2 .and. .not. ltempeq) no
! matter what BCbotm says, and a wall function needs a physically valid
! surface thls/qts, which this bare-bones case does not set (they stay at
! modsurfdata's placeholder default of -1 K / -1 kg/kg) -- that drove
! modthermodynamics::fromztop into a divide-by-zero at cold start. Matches
! tests/integration/nesting/namoptions.902's explicit BCbotm/BCtopm = 1.
!
! lrandomize defaults to .true. (src/modglobal.f90), so the cold start gets a
! small, deterministic (seeded by irandom), decomposition-independent velocity
! perturbation -- see randomize_field in src/modstartup.f90. That gives the
! driver-written planes actual, non-zero content instead of a trivial all-zero
! field, without needing an extra namelist block here.
!
! ktot = 32, not the 16 of tests/integration/nesting/namoptions.1012: the
! idriver == 1 monitor-file diagnostic in src/modtstep.f90 (around "elseif
! (idriver == 1)") hardcodes u0(irecydriver,1,32), so any grid with ktot < 32
! trips an out-of-bounds read of u0 under a bounds-checked (debug) build --
! a pre-existing latent bug in modtstep.f90, outside this fix's scope
! (modstartup.f90/moddriver.f90), worked around here by sizing the grid
! around it rather than fixed.
!
! test_driver_restart.py rewrites runtime, trestart, lwarmstart, startfile,
! nprocx and nprocy per run; every key it may rewrite must therefore stay
! present here even at a placeholder value (same convention as
! tests/integration/nesting/make_case_fixtures.py).

&RUN
iexpnr       = 903
runmode      = 1
runtime      = 1.
trestart     = 1.e9
dtmax        = 0.05
ladaptive    = .false.
libm         = .false.
lwarmstart   = .false.
startfile    = 'initd00000000_000_000.903'
nprocx       = 1
nprocy       = 1
/

&DOMAIN
itot         = 32
jtot         = 32
ktot         = 32
xlen         = 32.
ylen         = 32.
/

&BC
BCbotm       = 1
BCtopm       = 1
thls         = 288.
qts          = 0.
z0           = 0.05
z0h          = 0.05
/

&WALLS
iwallmom     = 1
/

&DYNAMICS
ipoiss       = 0
/

&DRIVER
idriver      = 1
tdriverstart = 0.25
dtdriver     = 0.05
driverstore  = 40
iplane       = 16
/

&INPS
zsize        = 32.
/
